{"term":"promise","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4f675d703324d4a14c","definition":"An oath or affirmation; a vow.","example":"When I make a promise, I always stick to it.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d410917f54db69fcb2","definition":"A transaction between two persons whereby the first person undertakes in the future to render some service or gift to the second person or devotes something valuable now and here to their use.","example":"He purſued Andrew Houſtoun upon his promiſe, to give him the like Sallary for the next year, and in abſence obtained him to be holden as confeſt and Decerned.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:28698c3c15a9c85eda","definition":"Something promised.","example":"That jewelry was a promise to me.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:996bb79ae2d1e69c4b","definition":"Reason to expect improvement or success; potential.","example":"His grade are poor, but I see promise in him.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6afc0e4256f84d341e","definition":"A placeholder object representing the eventual result of an asynchronous operation.","example":"You can often use observables instead of promises to deliver values asynchronously.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7d59e3bf4a7f00625","definition":"Bestowal or fulfillment of what is promised.","example":"It is time they receive their promise.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d271cfe6cd1af0e551","definition":"To commit to (some action or outcome), or to assure (a person) of such commitment; to make an oath or vow.","example":"\"You think that I'll take anything.\"\n\"I know you will, sweet.\" …\n\"There wasn't going to be any of that. You promised there wouldn't be.\"\n\"Well, there is now,\" she said sweetly.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["stipulate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, ditransitive","register":"ambitransitive, ditransitive","wordFamily":["a lick and a promise","a promise is a promise","a promise made is a promise kept","breach of promise","break a promise","break one's promise","break-promise","election promise","forepromise","lick and a promise","mispromise","on a promise","outpromise","overpromise","pinky promise","prepromise","promisable","promiseful","promiseless","promiser","promise ring","promise the earth","promise the moon","promise the stars","promise the world","repromise","underpromise","unpromise"],"source":"English